group gui/graph
note The graph canvas is derived, never accumulated. What is on screen is always a base plus an ordered list of expansions: the base is the selected path's steps as a tree, plus the focused symbol as its own root when no step shows it, and each expansion is 'the callers of X' or 'the callees of X' in the order the reader opened them. rebuild runs every frame and starts from empty, so closing an expansion also removes whatever was only reachable through it - there is no orphan cleanup because nothing is ever added incrementally. The only state that survives a rebuild is what the reader chose: the expansion list, which nodes are cut to a preview, how much context each shows, and any node they dragged. That state is keyed by symbol index, which a re-index invalidates, so save and restore carry it across one by symbol name.

