file src/gui/graph.rs
symbol Graph
lines 0 29
hash 5b8bdd4eac0c3347
note The fields split two ways, and the struct says which is which. The tree - nodes, their columns, positions, sizes, line ranges, step numbers, parents and origins, and the hit rectangles - is rebuilt every frame from the selection and is read as last frame's by the next frame's input. The reader's part survives frames: the expansions opened, the nodes cut to a preview or widened with context, the positions dragged (manual, which freezes the layout until the node set changes) and the camera. pos, size and manual are in cells and rows, cell is the cell width and row height in pixels, and hits are in window pixels. range is a node's own lines (the step's slice or the whole symbol) and view is that range widened by context and clamped to the file. step maps a step node to its pre-order position, anchor index and hierarchical number; origin maps an expansion node to the node that revealed it and whether it came through callees; code_top is the y of a node's first code row. auto_open is the off-path root whose callers and callees were opened for it; want_look asks to centre on the focus once it has a position, hold_look says the next focus change came from the graph itself and must not move the camera, want_fit asks for the fit, and keep is a node and its pixel position before the relayout its button caused.

